<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sergei Witte</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sergei Witte was a Russian statesman who served as minister of finance in the 1890s and early 1900s and later as prime minister. He promoted rapid industrialisation, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trans-siberian-railway">Trans-Siberian Railway</a> and the gold standard. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> profile notes that his programme drove high industrial growth rates in the 1890s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sergei-witte.jpg" alt="Sergei Witte" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chapiro, St. Petersburg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SergeiWitte01548v.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
